meta {
  name: Sync Site Admin Templates
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/opd-tests/sync
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "opdMasterDataId": "{{opdMasterDataId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  OPD equivalent of the lab **Sync Site Admin Templates** endpoint (POST /opd-tests/sync).
  
  Re-pull previously-imported lab tests from their SITE_ADMIN templates. Business
  JWT. Body: `opdMasterDataId` (required) + optional `opdTestIds` (subset; omit to
  sync every imported test in the master data).

  **Full overwrite:** each tenant copy's scalars are replaced from its template
  and its children (samples, params, reference ranges/values) are hard-deleted
  and recreated. Identity + provenance (`id`, `tenantId`, `branchId`,
  `opdMasterDataId`, `source`, `clonedFromId`) are preserved, `versionHistory` is
  bumped, and `templateSyncedAt` is stamped. Hand-created tests
  (`clonedFromId = null`) are never touched. Each test syncs in its own
  transaction. Returns:

  `{ "synced":  [{opdTestId,testName,templateId}],
     "skipped": [{opdTestId,testName,templateId,reason}],  // e.g. template removed
     "failed":  [{opdTestId,testName,templateId,reason}] }`

  - `opdMasterDataId` must belong to the caller's tenant → else 404
    `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND`.
}
